# Skill: mvp-specifier

Read and follow `skills/mvp-builder/mvp-specifier/SKILL.md`. Fill `skills/mvp-builder/mvp-specifier/templates/what-to-build.md` only.

Announce: `Using skill: mvp-specifier`.

## Job

Be the Elephant. Challenge the pitch. Write a self-contained `agent-engineer-skills/<name>/what-to-build.md`. Do not write code. Goldfish is a new Agent chat with `feature-developer`.

## Must

1. Announce the skill. Restate the pitch. Add nothing. If this is a feature in an existing app, refuse and name `feature-specifier`.
2. Ask only landmine questions that would make a Goldfish invent product. Always include the v1 / prototype cut unless already locked. Batch in `AskQuestion`. Do not only print A/B/C in the chat.
3. Feed pointed context in small blocks. Distill stack, layout, and constraints into the spec. Do not dump the whole repo. Do not scaffold.
4. Write every such decision into the specification. If the user will not answer, write `locked-default`. The developer may not pick another default.
5. Include prototype cut, context the implementer may use, in-scope, out-of-scope walls, behavior, done-when, and a do-not list.
6. Stop. Point at a new Agent chat and `feature-developer`. Do not start that skill here.

## Must not

- Write application code, scaffold, or boilerplate
- Start `feature-developer` or any other skill in this conversation
- Write `prd.md`, `clarification-log.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `concept.md`, or `notes.md`
- Leave "handle it appropriately" for the Goldfish
- Copy template coaching sentences into the output file
- Icons or emojis

## Do not use

When the request is a feature in an existing repo (`feature-specifier`), or they only want code, review, or tests on an existing specification.
